## Runtime Notes

- The controller owns fixed SCS Niagara components for Grass/Ground/Water and BeginPlay explicitly binds each channel RT asset variable into `User.RS_*_RT`.
- Legacy `RS_Water_RuntimeNiagara` is inspected for diagnostics only; the required production path is the fixed SCS `RS_Water_Niagara` component.
- The controller CDO now uses centered demo defaults: Grass `3000cm` with origin `[-1500,-1500,0]`, Water `4000cm` with origin `[-2000,-2000,0]`, Ground `4000cm` with origin `[-2000,-2000,0]`.
- Water foot pulses use a `0.18s` interval and alternate one traced foot per pulse. V45 uses continuous fractional history reprojection and raw material window origin; pixel-rounded recenter snapping is disabled.
- Water moving-wave defaults are `DefaultStrength=0.18`, `Damping=0.95`, `WaveSpeed=0.28`, `DefaultRadius=20cm`, and `ImpulseRadiusPixels=1.0`; V41 disables duplicate legacy SourceActive injection and V43 links every world-radius setter to the BP value.
- The smoke binds the explicit Piper actor, sets horizontal velocity before puddle contact, and moves it eight times while recording overlap/contact/pulse evidence.
- After compiling the Controller child class, the harness recompiles the Piper Child Actor parent and saves the demo map so PIE owns exactly one Controller instance.
- GPU readback discards a realtime prime read, disables Niagara component tick without `set_paused`, then requires two stable C++ `sample_render_target2d_region_stats` reads from the same region.
- Water is judged by normal RT channel deviation (`r > 0.501` or `g > 0.501`), not by the flat normal baseline.

## Debug Overlay Scope

- The Controller EventGraph now has a `bDebugDraw` branch that calls `PrintString` and `DrawDebugBox` without touching the normal 3-channel tick path.
- The persistent BP overlay is intentionally minimal in this pass: it proves the Controller-owned debug branch exists and compiles. Full selected/excluded source markers and dynamic per-channel counter text remain follow-up.

## Visual QA

Open `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Demo/L_RS_Demo`, press PIE, move the Piper pawn with WASD, and watch the three debug planes: Grass trail, Ground footprint mask, and Water normal ripple should update live.

